namespace Launchpad.Ui.Screens;

public static class LegalText
{
    public const string Updated = "Last updated November 16, 2026";

    public static readonly (string Heading, string Text)[] Terms =
    [
        ("Using MonkeForge", "MonkeForge is a community service for discovering and sharing Gorilla Tag mods. By using the service, you agree to these terms. Follow applicable laws and the rules of any games or platforms you use with downloaded mods. MonkeForge is not affiliated with Another Axiom."),
        ("Accounts and community conduct", "You can sign in with Discord, or with a username, email address and password, and you can add passkeys to either. You are responsible for your account and the content you submit. Do not impersonate others, harass users, misuse the service, bypass access controls, or upload malware or content that violates others’ rights."),
        ("Uploads and ownership", "Only upload content you own or have permission to share. You retain your rights and grant MonkeForge permission to store, display, and distribute your submitted content to operate the service. Any license supplied by a mod author governs use of that mod; a download does not transfer ownership."),
        ("Moderation", "Administrators may review, reject, or remove uploads and restrict accounts for violations or to protect the community. Availability of a mod does not guarantee that it is safe or compatible with your game."),
        ("Downloads and availability", "Mods and the service are provided as available, without guarantees of uninterrupted access, compatibility, or fitness for a particular purpose. Review a mod’s source, permissions, and author instructions before installing it. You are responsible for your choice to install and use mods. To the extent permitted by applicable law, MonkeForge is not responsible for losses caused by third-party mods or interruptions to the service. These terms do not limit rights that cannot legally be excluded."),
        ("Payments", "Payments on MonkeForge are processed by Stripe and are also subject to Stripe’s terms. For paid mods and memberships, the seller is the merchant and MonkeForge facilitates the sale. MonkeForge is the merchant for donations made to creators through MonkeForge and for donations to MonkeForge itself. Prices are shown in the listed currency and may not include taxes your bank or country adds."),
        ("Selling on MonkeForge", "To sell mods or offer memberships you must connect a Stripe account in good standing. By listing a paid mod or offering a membership tier, you authorize MonkeForge to host, display, distribute and deliver that content to buyers, including through encrypted injector delivery, and to collect payment on your behalf through your connected Stripe account. MonkeForge keeps a platform fee of 10% of every paid mod sale and every membership payment. Donations carry no platform fee. On sales and memberships, Stripe’s processing fee is taken from your share; on donations to you, MonkeForge covers it. You are responsible for the accuracy of your listing, for delivering the benefits you advertise, for your own taxes, and for keeping your Stripe account in good standing. Refunds and chargebacks on your sales come out of your Stripe balance."),
        ("Memberships", "Memberships renew every month and are charged automatically until you cancel. You can unsubscribe at any time from your profile. When you cancel, you keep access until the end of the month you already paid for and are not charged again. Except as described under Refunds and disputes, payments for time already started are not refunded. Sellers may change a tier’s price for new subscribers only; your price stays the same while your membership continues. If a seller retires a tier, your membership ends at the end of your current paid month."),
        ("Refunds and disputes", "If something goes wrong with a purchase or membership, you can open a dispute with MonkeForge staff from your profile within 90 days of the payment. Please try the creator first if it is something they can fix. MonkeForge reserves the right, at its sole discretion, to review disputes, to request information from buyers and sellers, to issue full or partial refunds on any sale or membership payment, and to cancel memberships. When MonkeForge accepts a dispute, the refund is returned from the seller’s Stripe balance and MonkeForge returns its platform fee. Opening a dispute with MonkeForge does not limit any rights you have with your bank or card issuer, but filing a chargeback may end your access to what you bought and any related memberships."),
        ("Takedowns and selling restrictions", "MonkeForge may, at any time, remove or unlist a paid mod, end its tiers, cancel the memberships attached to it, stop an account from selling, or suspend an account. We may do this for violations of these terms, suspected fraud, unusual dispute or chargeback rates, legal requests, risks to users, or to protect the service. When a paid mod or seller is taken down, active memberships connected to it are cancelled and no further payments are taken. Whether past payments are refunded is decided by MonkeForge staff case by case."),
        ("Licensed content and injector delivery", "Buying a mod or joining a membership gives you a personal, non-transferable license to use that content as allowed by its creator. It does not transfer ownership. Mods delivered through the injector may only be used through MonkeForge’s injector. You may not extract, copy, decompile, redistribute or resell them, or try to get around how they are delivered. Access can end if a payment is refunded or charged back, if a membership ends, or if the content is taken down."),
        ("Donations", "Donations are voluntary gifts to a creator or to MonkeForge. They do not buy access to any content or service and are generally not refundable, though MonkeForge may refund a donation at its discretion, for example if it was made by mistake."),
        ("Changes", "These terms may be updated as the service changes. Updates will appear on this page with a revised date. If you keep using MonkeForge after an update, including continuing a membership, you accept the updated terms."),
