    public static readonly (string Heading, string Text)[] Privacy =
    [
        ("Information stored", "When you sign in with Discord, MonkeForge receives your Discord user ID, username, display name, avatar information and, if Discord has verified it, your email address. Discord sign-in requests the identify and email scopes; it does not request your Discord password, server memberships, or bot access, and Discord access tokens are not persisted. Email accounts store your username, email address and a salted, slow hash of your password, never the password itself. Passkeys store only a public key. MonkeForge also stores account and profile information, appearance and email preferences, and content you submit, including mods, release files, images, descriptions, and profile links. Your email address is never shown publicly. It is used for account emails (confirmation links, password resets and security alerts), for notices when a release is uploaded to a mod you manage, and for announcements; you can turn the last two off in Settings -> Email or with the unsubscribe link in any of those emails."),
        ("How information is used", "Information supports sign-in, public author profiles, publishing, downloads, moderation, and saved settings. Administrators can access account information and moderation records to manage the service."),
        ("Public content", "Your public profile and approved uploads are visible to visitors. Files you publish can be downloaded and copied by others. Avoid including private information in profiles, descriptions, images, or uploaded files."),
        ("Cookies and browser storage", "A session cookie supports sign-in and request security. Browser local storage saves your selected accent color. You can clear these through your browser settings; clearing the session cookie signs you out, and clearing local storage resets browser preferences."),
        ("Activity data", "The application records mod view and download activity, including the mod, category, time, and country code when provided by a trusted proxy. These activity records do not store IP addresses or precise coordinates, and the application does not make third-party geolocation requests. Hosting infrastructure may process request information separately."),
        ("Payments", "Card payments are handled by Stripe. MonkeForge never receives your full card number. We store a record of what you paid for: the item or membership, amount, currency, date, payment status, and the Stripe IDs needed to look it up, refund it, or cancel it. For memberships we also store whether the membership is active and when it renews or ends. If you sell on MonkeForge, Stripe collects your identity and bank details directly. We store your Stripe account ID and whether it can accept payments, plus records of your sales, the platform fee, and refunds."),
        ("Disputes", "When you open a dispute, MonkeForge staff can see your reason, the payment it is about, and your account details. Staff may share relevant details with the seller and with Stripe to resolve it. Sellers are told when a refund is issued on one of their sales."),
        ("Injector devices", "If you install injector-delivered mods, we store each device you register: its name, a public key that identifies it, and when it was last used. Each install is logged with your account, the device, the mod version, the time, and a one-way hash of your IP address. We use this to limit how many devices can use a purchase, to prevent abuse, and to trace leaked copies."),
        ("External services", "Discord handles Discord sign-in, our email provider delivers email, and Stripe handles payments, each under its own privacy policy. Links to source code, author websites, and other external services are governed by those services’ policies."),
        ("Retention and your choices", "Account information, uploaded content, and activity records are stored to support operation of the service. Payment, refund, and dispute records are kept even if a mod is removed or an account is closed, because we may need them for accounting, tax, fraud prevention, or legal reasons. You can edit your profile and preferences and sign out at any time. For removal of information you cannot edit yourself, contact the site administrator through the community channel where you accessed MonkeForge. Removal from this service cannot remove copies others have downloaded."),
        ("Policy updates", "Changes to this policy will be posted here with a revised date."),
